--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [dcl.fct.def.default]/5: a special member function may be declared
in the class and explicitly defaulted on its first declaration outside it
(`template <class C> buf<C>::buf(const buf &) = default;'); it is then
user-provided but behaves as the implicit one. The front end reported
"unexpected statement: default" and dropped the copy constructor and the
copy assignment; the leftover `default' statement then reached symbolic
execution, which aborted ("symex_other.cpp: Unreachable") -- the same
abort as a leftover member_initializer (round 163e): an unconverted
statement was not rejected before symex. The out-of-line `= default' is
now represented like the in-class one (an empty body marked
#defaulted_function, which convert_function turns into the memberwise
copy). libstdc++'s basic_streambuf defines its copy constructor and copy
assignment this way (streambuf:835/840, the constructor declared at
streambuf:812), dropped in cpp11_ofstream_from_string and the goto-
programs TUs; test_libstdcxx.desc is that program and forbids only the
streambuf:812 drop. g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept both programs. Fails on
bin53.
